 in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s and then 1s between them (exponential backoff).\n\n- **Only 503 is retried.** Any other HTTP error, and any network error such as a timeout or refused connection, is raised straight away as before.\n- **If all 3 attempts get a 503,** the last 503 error is raised to the caller.\n- **The attempt count and base delay** are class settings (`MAX_ATTEMPTS`, `BACKOFF_BASE`), so they can be changed without editing the method.\n- **New optional argument:** the constructor now takes `sleep=time.sleep`, so a test can pass its own function and skip the real waits. Existing callers don't need to change anything.\n\nI checked it against a local test server:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Waits |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | JSON returned | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 503, 503, 503 | 503 raised; no 4th request made | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 500 | 500 raised | none |\n| 200 | JSON returned | none |\n\nI didn't add a test file; there are no tests in the repo yet.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34695, "requests_cache_write": 143650, "requests_cost_usd": 0.759657, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1721, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial28", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 115, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:52:40.058883+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 20.872, "t_checker_s": 19.233, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_m